      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\), where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we start by using Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas tell us that for the polynomial \\(x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), the sums and products of the roots are given by:\n\\[\nr + s + t = -a, \\quad rs + rt + st = b, \\quad rst = -c.\n\\]\nFor the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we have \\(a = -20\\), \\(b = 18\\), and \\(c = -7\\). Therefore, by Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20, \\quad rs + rt + st = 18, \\quad rst = 7.\n\\]\nWe need to find the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\). Expanding the product, we have:\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + (r + s + t) + (rs + rt + st) + rst.\n\\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
