    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We are given the polynomial equation \\( x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0 \\) and asked to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of this polynomial.\n\nFirst, we use Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots. For the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7\\), Vieta's formulas tell us:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). We expand this expression:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + rs + st.\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by grouping the terms:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + (rs+rt+st).\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 18 = 57.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
